---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero from '~/components/widgets/Hero.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Terms of Service',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <Hero>
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Terms of <span class="text-accent dark:text-white">Service</span>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      <span class="text-lg"> Last updated: September 11, 2026 </span>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <!-- Terms Content -->
  <section class="px-4 py-16 mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8">Last Updated: September 11, 2026</p>

      <p>
        Welcome to 123 ToDo. These Terms of Service ("Terms") constitute a legally binding agreement between you
        ("User," "you," or "your") and <strong>Unforgettable Management Ltd</strong> ("Company," "we," "us," or "our"), governing
        your access to and use of the 123 ToDo website (<a
          href="https://www.123todo.com"
          class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">123todo.com</a
        >), web application (<a href="https://app.123todo.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">app.123todo.com</a
        >), Progressive Web App (PWA), and associated software, services, and features (collectively, the "Service").
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>PLEASE READ THESE TERMS CAREFULLY.</strong> By accessing, browsing, installing, or using the Service, you
        acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms and our Privacy Policy. If you do
        not agree with any part of these Terms, you must immediately discontinue using the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Architecture & Nature of the Service</h2>
      <p>
        123 ToDo is a local-first, privacy-focused productivity and task organization tool implementing the 1-2-3 daily
        focus methodology (Must Do, Should Do, Could Do).
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Local-First Client-Side Operation:</strong> By architectural design, all tasks, notes, timestamp logs, subtasks,
        project labels, custom settings, and attached photographs entered into the Service are stored directly and locally
        on your physical device using your web browser's storage engines (including IndexedDB and LocalStorage). Under default
        operation, <strong
          >we do not operate application servers that store, process, or retain your unencrypted task data</strong
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Zero-Knowledge End-to-End Encrypted Cloud Sync (Optional):</strong> The Service provides optional multi-cloud
        synchronization features (supporting Cloudflare Workers KV, Google Drive, and custom WebDAV servers). When activated,
        your data is cryptographically encrypted directly on your device using military-grade <strong
          >AES-256-GCM zero-knowledge encryption</strong
        >
        via the Web Crypto API, derived from a master passphrase known only to you. Decryption keys and unencrypted data
        are never transmitted to, visible to, or stored on our servers or third-party storage hosts.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Voice Dictation ("Talk"):</strong> Voice transcription features utilize your web browser's native Web Speech
        API engine. Voice audio is processed locally or through your browser vendor's platform speech service; 123 ToDo never
        records, intercepts, or stores your voice audio.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No Account Required & No Identity Verification</h2>
      <p>
        The core Service operates without requiring user registration, email submission, account creation, or identity
        verification. You may access the Service anonymously. Because we do not maintain accounts or verify identities,
        we have no means to identify you, locate your device, or associate you with any specific dataset.
      </p>

      <h2>3. TOTAL DISCLAIMER OF LIABILITY FOR DATA LOSS</h2>
      <div class="p-6 bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-950/30 rounded-xl border-2 border-red-500/40 my-6">
        <p class="font-bold text-red-900 dark:text-red-200 uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-2">
          CRITICAL NOTICE — SOLE USER RESPONSIBILITY FOR DATA BACKUP
        </p>
        <p class="text-red-950 dark:text-red-100 text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <strong
            >TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL UNFORGETTABLE MANAGEMENT LTD, ITS
            DIRECTORS, OFFICERS, EMPLOYEES, CONTRACTORS, AFFILIATES, OR LICENSORS BE HELD LIABLE FOR ANY DATA LOSS, DATA
            CORRUPTION, UNRECOVERABILITY, ACCIDENTAL DELETION, OR INABILITY TO ACCESS DATA, REGARDLESS OF CAUSE OR LEGAL
            THEORY (WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT, NEGLIGENCE, STRICT LIABILITY, OR OTHERWISE).</strong
          >
        </p>
        <p class="text-red-950 dark:text-red-100 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-0">
          You explicitly understand and agree that you are solely responsible for maintaining regular, independent,
          off-device backups of all your data (using the built-in manual JSON export feature).
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Without limiting the generality of the foregoing, we shall have <strong>zero liability</strong> for any data loss,
        erasure, destruction, or corruption resulting from:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Browser Actions & Cache Clearing:</strong> Clearing browser history, cookies, site data, or cache; resetting
          or uninstalling your browser; or using Private / Incognito browsing modes which automatically discard storage upon
          closing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Operating System Eviction:</strong> Storage reclamation, automated cache purging, or disk cleanup triggered
          by your operating system (e.g. iOS, Android, macOS, or Windows) under low-disk-space or battery-saving conditions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hardware Events:</strong> Device loss, theft, hardware failure, water damage, screen breakage, factory
          resets, or physical destruction.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Forgotten Encryption Passphrases:</strong> Because cloud sync utilizes authentic Zero-Knowledge AES-256-GCM
          encryption, your master passphrase is known solely to you. If you lose, misplace, or forget your encryption passphrase,
          <strong>your synced data is mathematically impossible to recover</strong>. We have no master key, back door,
          or recovery mechanism, and cannot assist you with password resets under any circumstances.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloud & Network Failures:</strong> Network outages, synchronization race conditions, clock drift between
          devices, cloud host downtime, API quota exhaustions, or service suspensions by third-party providers (including
          Cloudflare, Google Drive, or WebDAV hosts).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Software & Database Glitches:</strong> Unforeseen browser bugs, WebKit/Chromium engine regressions, IndexedDB
          schema corruptions, or software updates.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Commercial Rights, Paid Features & Future Monetisation</h2>
      <p>
        While 123 ToDo currently provides free access to its core client-side features, <strong
          >Unforgettable Management Ltd expressly reserves the unrestricted right, at its sole discretion, to monetise
          the Service or any component, tier, or feature thereof at any point in the future.</strong
        >
      </p>
      <p>Such future monetisation may include, without limitation:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Introducing optional paid subscription tiers (such as "Pro", "Team", or "Enterprise" plans);</li>
        <li>
          Restricting certain advanced features, multi-device cloud sync quotas, or enhanced storage tools to paying
          subscribers;
        </li>
        <li>Introducing one-time lifetime license purchases, in-app purchases, or commercial licensing;</li>
        <li>Establishing fair-use capacity limits on free tier usage;</li>
        <li>Partnering with trusted, relevant productivity partners or sponsors.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>No Grandfathered Free Entitlement:</strong> The availability of any feature, service, or functionality on
        a free basis today does not grant, convey, or guarantee any permanent, perpetual, or irrevocable right to continued
        free access in the future.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Notice & Data Portability Guarantee:</strong> In the event that previously free core features become subject
        to a mandatory fee, we will provide reasonable advance notice on our website or within the application. Furthermore,
        we guarantee that you will <strong
          >always retain the uninterrupted right and technical ability to export your complete data as a standard, open
          JSON file free of charge</strong
        > before any mandatory paid requirements take effect.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Optional Cloud Sync — Third-Party Terms</h2>
      <p>When you enable optional multi-cloud sync:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Drive Sync:</strong> Your encrypted backup is stored within your personal Google Drive account.
          You must comply with Google's Terms of Service and Privacy Policy. We are not responsible for Google service disruptions,
          account deactivations, or API modifications. You may revoke 123 ToDo's OAuth token anytime via your Google Security
          console.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare Workers KV:</strong> Encrypted blobs synced via our Cloudflare edge worker are stored in ciphertext
          format. While Cloudflare provides high availability, we provide no uptime SLA or warranty against transmission
          drops.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Custom WebDAV:</strong> If you connect an independent WebDAV server (such as Nextcloud or Synology), you
          are solely responsible for maintaining the availability, SSL certificates, storage capacity, and security of that
          server.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Acceptable Use & User Conduct</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to use the Service strictly in compliance with all applicable local, national, and international laws.
        You agree not to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the Service for any unlawful, fraudulent, defamatory, or malicious purpose;</li>
        <li>
          Attempt to interfere with, disrupt, overload, or compromise the integrity or security of the Service, edge
          CDN, or sync endpoints;
        </li>
        <li>
          Deploy automated scrapers, bots, spiders, or scripts that subject our infrastructure to unreasonable load;
        </li>
        <li>
          Attempt to reverse engineer, decompile, dissemble, or extract the proprietary source code or intellectual
          property of the Service for competitive commercial reproduction.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
      <p>
        The Service, including but not limited to its software code, user interface designs, logos, artwork, icons,
        sound effects, algorithms, documentation, trademarks, and branding (the "Company IP"), is the exclusive property
        of <strong>Unforgettable Management Ltd</strong> and is protected by United Kingdom, European, and international
        copyright, trademark, and intellectual property laws.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are granted a personal, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and limited license to access and use
        the Service solely for your personal or internal business productivity in accordance with these Terms. You
        retain all ownership rights to the content, text, and photos you enter into the application.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Disclaimer of Warranties ("AS IS" & "AS AVAILABLE")</h2>
      <p>
        <strong
          >THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED ON AN "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" BASIS WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS
          OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
          PURPOSE, TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, ACCURACY, FREEDOM FROM BUGS, UNINTERRUPTED AVAILABILITY, OR SECURITY.</strong
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not warrant that the Service will meet your specific requirements, operate error-free, be free from
        malicious code, or that any defects will be identified or corrected. Any reliance you place on the Service for
        mission-critical deadlines, medical reminders, or legal obligations is undertaken entirely at your own risk.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Overall Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        <strong
          >TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL UNFORGETTABLE MANAGEMENT LTD, ITS DIRECTORS,
          EMPLOYEES, OR PARTNERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, CONSEQUENTIAL, INCIDENTAL, EXEMPLARY, PUNITIVE, OR SPECIAL
